# Walkthrough — Frontend Direct Answer Rendering Fix & Rebuild

## 1. Root Cause Identification

### Identified Bug
In [`templates/index.html`](file:///c:/github/textline/templates/index.html), a duplicated, malformed HTML fragment (`<div class="prov-item">...`) had been pasted directly inside the main `<script>` tag within the `addHistoryItem` JavaScript function.

### Execution Path & Symptom
1. When the browser loaded `index.html`, the JavaScript engine encountered HTML tags (`</div>`, `<div class="prov-item">`) inside the `<script>` block.
2. This threw an unhandled JavaScript **`SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<'`**, aborting execution of the script.
3. Because script initialization halted before registering or executing event listeners, when WebSocket emitted `status_update` with `data.answer` (containing `<!DOCTYPE html>...`):
   - The `#answer-text` element remained hidden (`display: none`).
   - The direct answer panel appeared visually blank/empty except for placeholder graphics.

---

## 2. Changes Implemented

### Files Changed
1. **[`templates/index.html`](file:///c:/github/textline/templates/index.html)**:
   - Removed the malformed HTML snippet from inside the JavaScript function `addHistoryItem()`.
   - Confirmed `#answer-text` uses `answerText.textContent = data.answer;` on `<pre id="answer-text">`, ensuring responses containing `<!DOCTYPE html>` or HTML/code source are safely rendered as plain text without live DOM execution.
   - Added `overflow-y: auto` and `max-height: 400px` to `.answer-box` and `.answer-text` to ensure long responses and 50-line padding scroll cleanly.
2. **[`test_fallback_system.py`](file:///c:/github/textline/test_fallback_system.py)**:
   - Added **Test 34** (`test_34_doctype_html_rendering_and_clipboard_preservation`) specifically asserting that responses beginning with `<!DOCTYPE html>` format cleanly, preserve raw text, and bind properly to `answerText.textContent`.

